All this looks pretty straightforward, but apparently there is still some confusion about
the limitations of the classical equations of motion, even among experts in eﬀective the-
ories. For example, statements such as “the operators that vanish by the equations of
motion are redundant” or “the operators that vanish by the equations of motion give
no contribution to on-shell matrix elements”, without further qualiﬁcation, are found ev-
