(and S2) the equation of motion to second order in λ does not give, in general, an action
that is equivalent to S to second order. The same conclusions apply to the case in which
the equations of motion of S′ are used in S1 (and S2), as can be seen by exchanging the
roles of S and S′ and considering the inverse transformation. To obtain the correct S′, it is
necessary to perform the actual ﬁeld redeﬁnition in every term of the original action. This
can be done either directly or using the functional-derivative expansion in the second line
of eq. (5.2).
5.2
Power counting
The eﬀective ﬁeld theories of interest often depend on several parameters, which can be
taken to be the cutoﬀscale Λ and additional dimensionless quantities, such as coupling
constants, ratios of masses and 4π factors associated to loops.
The eﬀective theory is
