x, by translation on x:
t · (ax2 + 2bx + c) := a(x + t)2 + 2b(x + t) + c = ax2 + 2(ax + b)t + at2 + 2bt + c.
Then all orbits are closed, and contained in the ﬁbers of the map
π : C3 −→C2,
(a, b, c) 7−→(a, ac −b2).
Speciﬁcally, the ﬁber over (x, y) consists of one orbit if x ̸= 0, and of two orbits if x = 0 but y ̸= 0;
all these orbits have trivial isotropy group. Moreover, the ﬁber over (0, 0) is the line ℓdeﬁned by
b = c = 0, and consisting of the G-ﬁxed points. It follows that C(X)G = C(a, ac −b2) and that
