+# Batch 16 authoring notes — Finite-Order EFT Operator Spaces and Redundancies
+
+## Plan and batch reconciliation
+
+The assigned design is § “Finite-Order EFT Operator Spaces and Redundancies” at L219–235 of `research/plan-advanced-qft-and-supersymmetry-track.md`. The current `research/plan-spec.json` row and `research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-16.pages.json` agree with that design on both page IDs, title, order 972, category/library, companion relation, and the two A-page requirements. Their empty item arrays are initial placeholders; the design's five planned item IDs remain assigned.
+
+One stale scaffold mismatch is recorded: the `qftx-eft-operator-quotients` object in `research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/scaffold/proposed-inventory.json` lists only `aqft-susy-math-foundations` under `requires`, while both the complete design and active plan also require `reductive-affine-invariant-theory-and-geometric-quotients`. The plan controls. The active manifest keeps both page requirements; no global plan or imported page is edited.
+
+The older machine inventory lists three invariant-theory items as nonlogical supplier candidates. The owner disposition in `research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-owner-resolution/owner-acceptance.md` and its bounded `invariant-review.md` accepts the exact imported reductive/Reynolds proof context for this run, while preserving the originals' historical publication stamps. This batch uses only the finite-dimensional rational-module exactness actually needed. It does not use the affine invariant-ring finite-generation theorem or the invariant-subring ideal lemma: those commutative-ring results do not establish facts about a Grassmann algebra, arbitrary relation subspace, or infinite jets.
+
+## Dependency graph and levels before authoring
+
+The run record `research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-dependency-levels.json` assigns batch 16 level **1**, with the sole in-run batch requirement **1**. The A/B page edge is recorded separately from item-level logical edges.
+
+The authored inventory is eight items: seven A-page items and one B-page example. Item levels count only in-run logical item suppliers; imported/published mathematical context does not raise an item level.
+
+| Item | Direct item dependencies | Planned item level |
+|---|---|---:|
+| `def-aqft-local-operator-and-dimension` | `def-reductive-and-linearly-reductive-over-c` (external) | 0 |
+| `lem-aqft-finite-order-local-operator-space-finite-dimensional` | `def-aqft-local-operator-and-dimension` | 1 |
+| `lem-aqft-invariant-quotient-exactness` | `def-reductive-and-linearly-reductive-over-c`, `thm-complete-reducibility-and-reynolds-operator-for-complex-reductive-group`, `def-axiom-of-choice` (all external) | 0 |
