+| `prop-aqft-integration-by-parts-eom-and-field-redefinition-redundancy` | `def-aqft-operator-basis-quotient`, `lem-aqft-invariant-quotient-exactness`, `def-axiom-of-choice` | 3 |
+| `def-aqft-lsz-amplitude-data` | `def-aqft-local-operator-and-dimension` | 1 |
+| `thm-aqft-field-redefinition-observable-equivalence-at-fixed-order` | `def-aqft-operator-basis-quotient`, `prop-aqft-integration-by-parts-eom-and-field-redefinition-redundancy`, `def-aqft-lsz-amplitude-data`, `def-axiom-of-choice` | 4 |
+| `ex-aqft-operator-basis-reduction` | `def-aqft-operator-basis-quotient`, `prop-aqft-integration-by-parts-eom-and-field-redefinition-redundancy`, `def-axiom-of-choice` | 4 |
+
+Before authoring, `loadStep1Record` and `step1Decision` were called for the planned batch-1 supersymmetry-foundations items. Their current readiness records are missing; that fact alone is not treated as a prerequisite defect. The actual page carrier `library/quantum-field-theory-mathematics/aqft-susy-math-foundations.md` is absent and the batch-1 manifest still has an empty item inventory. This is a genuine unresolved **page-level** prerequisite edge. No batch-16 item consumes a statement from that page: the EFT operator algebra is independently defined and proved here. Authoring continues without inserting an invented superalgebra premise. The A-page cross-batch row remains `open`, and the final readiness decision records this exact page dependency.
+
+The other required A-page supplier is the published reductive affine invariant-theory page. Its current page bytes and `thm-complete-reducibility-and-reynolds-operator-for-complex-reductive-group` item bytes match both the local import pins and the read-only originals. The theorem's exact consumed clause is finite-dimensional complete reducibility and the natural Reynolds projection, including surjectivity of invariants under an equivariant surjection. The theorem explicitly assumes full AC; every local consumer of that clause records `def-axiom-of-choice` and the use in its Facts/contract. The original `verification.judge` stamp remains unchanged and is not represented as an independent publication audit.
+
+## Claim, conventions, and exact scope
+
+The A page defines local operators in a finite-dimensional, rationally acted jet-polynomial superalgebra over `C`, with finitely many field species, a finite derivative cutoff, a finite maximum polynomial degree, a fixed coefficient convention, and a fixed finite weight/order. The fixed-weight space is proved finite-dimensional by `lem-aqft-finite-order-local-operator-space-finite-dimensional`; the polynomial-degree cutoff also covers weight-zero field coordinates without an infinite-dimensional completion claim. The invariant relation space is the explicitly declared sum/intersection of algebraic, integration-by-parts, leading-EOM, and allowed field-redefinition directions. The quotient is exactly by these declared relations; no completeness claim for every possible EFT redundancy is inferred.
+
+The local exactness result `lem-aqft-invariant-quotient-exactness` proves the canonical map from invariant operators modulo invariant relations to invariant classes in the raw quotient, using only the exact finite rational-module statement of the imported complete-reducibility/Reynolds theorem. The field-redefinition proposition treats one chosen order at a time in a finite truncated formal parameter, requires the stated compact-support/no-boundary functional convention, and includes the higher-order remainder. The later theorem states quantum on-shell amplitude equivalence only for a specified finite regulator, transformed measure/Jacobian and sources, and a stable-particle LSZ data set with simple poles and nonzero overlaps. It makes no continuum-limit, anomaly-free Jacobian, arbitrary off-shell Green-function, or generic physical-QFT claim.
+
+The B example is the fixed four-dimensional natural-unit scalar model with one even field, a declared mass and quartic coefficient, compactly supported variations, and the dimension-six density `phi^2 (d phi)^2`. It computes its integration-by-parts and leading-EOM class and the exact order-`Lambda^-2` field redefinition, including the induced dimension-four and dimension-six coefficient shifts. It does not classify a SMEFT basis or infer data from a physical model.
+
+## Full-text source record
+
+The four sources and item-by-item dispositions are recorded in `research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-16.source-coverage.json`. Full relevant text was inspected in Burgess, *Introduction to Effective Field Theory*, §2.2.1–2.2.5 and §2.1's redundant-interaction argument; Neubert, *Effective Field Theory and Heavy Quark Physics*, §2; Criado–Pérez-Victoria, §§2–3, §5.1 and Appendix B; and Brion, Theorems 1.23–1.24. `source-fetch-check --stamp` passed **4/4** full-text fetches with no failure or drop. Burgess/Neubert support EFT dimensions, fixed-order operators and leading-EOM conventions; Criado–Pérez-Victoria supplies the exact regulator/Jacobian/source/LSZ caveats and higher-order warning; Brion supports only the imported Reynolds/complete-reducibility input. None is substituted for the local finite-space, quotient, variational, or LSZ conditional proofs.
+
+The previously harvested Warsaw-basis paper by Grzadkowski et al. is not used to claim a complete dimension-six basis or a count: the assigned scope is the generic finite relation quotient, and the source note records only its abstract and introduction as previously inspected. No SMEFT enumeration is inferred.
+
+## Completed item: `def-aqft-local-operator-and-dimension`
+
+Claim and conventions: defines a finite four-dimensional Minkowski jet-polynomial model with $\eta=(-,+,+,+)$, $x^0=ct$, natural units $c=\hbar=1$, a finite field-species list, explicit even/odd finite-dimensional field representations of a complex reductive algebraic group, finite jet order, field-degree cutoff, rational engineering weights, the supercommutative polynomial algebra, and $C\mathcal O_D/\Lambda^{D-4}$. The definition distinguishes formal complex operator spaces from any additional reality condition on a physical action. Its finite generator/degree cutoffs also permit weight-zero fields without silently claiming an infinite-dimensional homogeneous component.
+
+Exact dependency: `def-reductive-and-linearly-reductive-over-c`, `mathematical-premise`; no in-run item supplier, so `dependency_level: 0`. The imported definition's exact fixed-vector unipotence/reductivity convention was read; its local pin and original source hash match. Burgess, *Introduction to Effective Field Theory*, §2.2.1–2.2.5 and §2.1's redundant-interaction passage, <https://arxiv.org/pdf/hep-th/0701053>, and Neubert, *Effective Field Theory and Heavy Quark Physics*, §2, <https://arxiv.org/pdf/hep-ph/0512222>, support the fixed-order Wilsonian operator and engineering-dimension conventions. Exact read extents and limitations are in the batch-16 source-coverage JSON; source-fetch-check passed 4/4.
+
+Its proof-contract entry will record the definition class, exact dependency, source support, and boundary dispositions; no proof steps apply. The batch manifest row will preserve its complete uninterrupted Definition as the claim. No scoped validators have run yet. The item is draft with `verification.precheck: pending` until the final scoped formatter/precheck pass. The missing batch-1 A/B carrier remains the exact open A-page prerequisite row; it is not an item-level premise. Next: author and prove `lem-aqft-finite-order-local-operator-space-finite-dimensional`, then the generic invariant-quotient exactness lemma before using either in the operator quotient definition/proposition.
+
+## Completed item: `lem-aqft-finite-order-local-operator-space-finite-dimensional`
+
+Claim and conventions: with a finite graded jet generator basis, finite maximum polynomial field degree $q$, and fixed engineering weight $D$, the supercommutative monomial span is finite-dimensional; every parity- and weight-preserving invariant subspace is then finite-dimensional. The proof bounds all generator exponents by $q$, treats the zero-generator and empty-weight-component cases, and does not assume positive engineering weight for every field. Exact dependency: `def-aqft-local-operator-and-dimension`, `mathematical-premise`; `dependency_level: 1`. Burgess, §3's opening power-counting passage, printed p. 28, and Neubert, §2, PDF pp. 5–8, support the fixed-order EFT context only; neither is cited as proving the finite-monomial argument. The source coverage records those limits and the 4/4 full-text fetch result. No scoped validators have run yet; `verification.precheck` remains pending until final checks. The missing batch-1 page remains an open page-level edge. Next: author `lem-aqft-invariant-quotient-exactness` with its exact AC/Reynolds hypotheses, then the operator quotient definition and action-level proposition.
+
+## Completed item: `lem-aqft-invariant-quotient-exactness`
+
+Claim: for a complex reductive affine algebraic group $G$, full AC, a finite-dimensional rational $G$-module $V$, and a $G$-stable subspace $N$, the quotient map induces a surjection $V^G\to(V/N)^G$ with kernel $V^G\cap N$, hence a canonical isomorphism $V^G/(V^G\cap N)\cong(V/N)^G$. Exact dependencies are `def-reductive-and-linearly-reductive-over-c`, `thm-complete-reducibility-and-reynolds-operator-for-complex-reductive-group`, and `def-axiom-of-choice`, all mathematical premises; `dependency_level: 0` because each is outside this run. The actual theorem statement and complete proof were inspected, including the finite-dimensional rational-module scope, Reynolds naturality, surjectivity of invariants, and explicit AC assumption. Current imported item, page, AC, and reductive-definition hashes match `research/math-imports.json` and the read-only source originals. The source treatment is Brion, Theorems 1.23–1.24, printed pp. 8–9, full PDF <https://ccirm.centre-mersenne.org/item/10.5802/ccirm.1.pdf>; fetched and read here. Owner context disposition and the imported item's judge-only historical stamp are recorded above without conflating them. No other invariant-ring supplier is used. No scoped validators have run yet; precheck remains pending. The missing batch-1 page edge remains open. Next: define the operator quotient using the finite local space, then prove the IBP/EOM/field-redefinition proposition using this exactness lemma.
+
+## Completed item: `def-aqft-operator-basis-quotient`
+
+Claim and conventions: for the finite raw polynomial space $W_D$ at fixed jet order, field degree, and engineering weight, the invariant scalar subspace is $V_D=W_D^G$. Given a specified $G$-stable raw identity subspace $\widetilde R_D$, its invariant relations are $R_D=\widetilde R_D\cap V_D$ and the exact declared basis quotient is $V_D/R_D$. The definition keeps the raw space distinct from its invariant subspace so the following exactness lemma can identify this with invariant classes in $W_D/\widetilde R_D$. Direct dependencies are `def-aqft-local-operator-and-dimension` and `lem-aqft-finite-order-local-operator-space-finite-dimensional`, both `mathematical-premise`; `dependency_level: 2`. The quotient is exactly by the specified relation subspace and makes no exhaustive all-EFT redundancy claim. Burgess §2.1–2.2, Neubert §2, and Criado–Pérez-Victoria §§3/5.1 are context sources only; the local definition and subsequent proof determine the exact relation class. All four full-text sources remain fetch-verified; no scoped validators have run. The batch-1 A-page edge remains open. Next: author the action-level proposition and specify the boundary functional, leading variational derivative, and one-order formal field-redefinition convention.
+
+## Completed item: `prop-aqft-integration-by-parts-eom-and-field-redefinition-redundancy`
+
+Claim and conventions: for the finite rational $G$-module $W_D$ and its $G$-stable relation span, the invariant quotient is canonically the invariant part of the raw quotient, using the exactness lemma under full AC. A specified boundary functional annihilates compactly supported total divergences. A left Euler derivative for odd fields and ordinary Euler derivative for even fields is defined by the first-variation identity. For a $G$-equivariant, parity-compatible, compact-support-preserving local variation $F$ and finite formal action $S_\epsilon=S_0+\cdots+\epsilon^NS_N$, the explicit map $\phi\mapsto\phi-\epsilon^kF$ is constructed to be invertible modulo $\epsilon^{N+1}$ and changes the action by $-\epsilon^k\mathcal I(F^a\mathcal E_a^{(0)})+O(\epsilon^{k+1})$. It removes the matching EOM term at order $k$ while retaining the higher-order terms generated by the full pullback. This proves action-level fixed-order equivalence only.
+
+Direct dependencies: `def-aqft-local-operator-and-dimension`, `def-aqft-operator-basis-quotient`, `lem-aqft-invariant-quotient-exactness`, and `def-axiom-of-choice`, all `mathematical-premise`; `dependency_level: 3` because the operator quotient definition is the highest in-run supplier at level 2. Full AC is stated in the item, tied to the imported Reynolds exactness use, and carried as a direct dependency. Source context: Burgess §2.1, equations (21)–(26), and §2.2; Neubert §2, equations (27)–(29); Criado–Pérez-Victoria §§3 and 5.1. Their full-text locators, exact per-item extents, and limitations are in the batch-16 source-coverage JSON; all four fetch stamps remain current. No scoped validators have run. The exact batch-1 page edge is still open. Next: author `def-aqft-lsz-amplitude-data`, then prove the conditional fixed-order LSZ amplitude theorem.
+
+## Completed item: `def-aqft-lsz-amplitude-data`
+
+Claim and conventions: defines a finite-dimensional regulated generating functional with a nonzero partition-function unit, a local identity-leading coordinate map with its exact measure Jacobian and transformed source, and a conditional LSZ datum consisting of connected momentum-space functions, stable one-particle simple poles, nonzero residues, invertible transformed overlap data, and normalized joint pole extraction. The LSZ/continuum data are assumptions to a later theorem, not a claim that such limits exist for a generic EFT. Dependency: `def-aqft-local-operator-and-dimension`, `mathematical-premise`; `dependency_level: 1`. Source: Criado–Pérez-Victoria, §2, PDF pp. 6–8, equations (2.2)–(2.8), read in full; its exact support and limits are in the source-coverage JSON (`https://arxiv.org/pdf/1811.09413`). No scoped validators have run; precheck remains pending. The batch-1 page edge remains open. Next: prove `thm-aqft-field-redefinition-observable-equivalence-at-fixed-order`, including the regulator Jacobian/source change and the LSZ residue normalization.
+
+## Completed item: `thm-aqft-field-redefinition-observable-equivalence-at-fixed-order`
+
+Claim and conventions: under full AC, a local identity-leading formal field-coordinate map, an exact regulated change-of-variables identity including its Jacobian, a source transformed by the same map, and a common limit with stable simple one-particle poles, the normalized source functionals and their normalized joint-residue amplitudes agree coefficientwise through finite order $N$. The theorem states the LSZ pole factorization and mass-shell convention $s=-\eta^{\mu\nu}p_\mu p_\nu$ with $\eta=(-,+,+,+)$; it excludes dropped Jacobians, unchanged sources, discarded higher-order terms, unstable external states, and nonexistent limits. It does not assert equality of off-shell action expressions.
+
+Direct dependencies: `def-aqft-operator-basis-quotient`, `prop-aqft-integration-by-parts-eom-and-field-redefinition-redundancy`, `def-aqft-lsz-amplitude-data`, `def-axiom-of-choice`, and `def-reductive-and-linearly-reductive-over-c`, all mathematical premises; `dependency_level: 4`. Full AC is stated and directly carried through the quotient/action premise. Source: Criado–Pérez-Victoria, §2, PDF pp. 6–8, equations (2.2)–(2.8), and Appendix B, PDF pp. 33–34, including the measure/source transformation, LSZ interpolator, and multiple-EOM-insertion boundary. Exact per-item extent and limitations are in the batch-16 source-coverage JSON at <https://arxiv.org/pdf/1811.09413>. No scoped validators have run; this theorem remains draft with precheck pending. The batch-1 page edge remains open. Next: author the worked B-page scalar operator reduction, then synchronize the manifests, contracts, coverage, cross-batch row, and Step-1 readiness records.
+
+## Completed item: `ex-aqft-operator-basis-reduction`
+
+Claim and conventions: for a compactly supported real scalar on $\mathbb R^{1,3}$ with mostly-plus metric, natural units, $m\geq0$, dimensionless $g,C,\epsilon$, and an order-$\Lambda^{-2}$ correction $C\mathcal O_6/\Lambda^2$, the finite quotient includes the total divergence and leading-EOM generator $\phi^3\mathcal E_0$. Direct differentiation and integration by parts give $[\mathcal O_6]=-m^2[\phi^4]/3-g[\phi^6]/18$. The identity-leading redefinition $\phi\mapsto\phi+\epsilon C\phi^3/(3\Lambda^2)$ removes the dimension-six operator and shifts the two other dimension-six densities by the stated coefficients modulo $\epsilon^2$. The example is a formal mathematical action calculation; it does not assert a physical realization or an LSZ/S-matrix result.
+
+Direct dependencies are `def-aqft-local-operator-and-dimension`, `def-aqft-operator-basis-quotient`, `prop-aqft-integration-by-parts-eom-and-field-redefinition-redundancy`, and `def-axiom-of-choice`, all mathematical premises; the highest in-run supplier is the proposition at level 3, so `dependency_level: 4`. Full text: Burgess §2.1, equations (25)–(26), <https://arxiv.org/pdf/hep-th/0701053>; Neubert §2, equations (27)–(29), <https://arxiv.org/pdf/hep-ph/0512222>; Criado–Pérez-Victoria §3/Appendix B, <https://arxiv.org/pdf/1811.09413>, as scope context only. The local calculation recomputes all signs and coefficients; full extents/limits are in the source-coverage record. No scoped validators have run; precheck remains pending. The missing batch-1 page edge remains open. Next: synchronize A/B pages and manifest inventories, build all proof-contract and coverage rows, record the open page edge, compute item levels, and create readiness records after scoped checks.
